[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "Queen's Gambit"]
[Variation "Slav Defense: Alapin Variation"]
[ECO "D16"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "keep-the-pawn,a4-guard"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "main"]
[Opponent "2...c6"]
[Start "orthodox 2.c4"]

2... c6 3. Nf3 { Develops and keeps the pawn on e2 where it can still go to e3 or e4. } 3... Nf6 4. Nc3 { A second piece aimed at the centre. Black must decide what to do about the pawn on c4. } 4... dxc4 ( 4... e6 5. e3 Nbd7 6. Bd3 ) 5. a4 { Stops ...b5, so Black cannot defend the extra pawn on c4. White will take it back when it suits. See [the position](rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/P1pP4/2N2N2/1P2PPPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq -). [%csl Rb5] } 5... Bf5 ( 5... Bg4 6. Ne5 ) 6. e3 { Opens the f1 bishop to take on c4 and guards d4. } 6... e6 7. Bxc4 { Retakes the pawn. Black's bishop on f5 has no good way to challenge White's centre. } 7... Bb4 8. O-O { Castles, so the king is safe before Black's bishop pins the knight on c3. } 8... Nbd7 9. Qe2 { Guards the knight on c3 and the bishop on c4, and clears the way for e4. } 9... Bg6 10. e4 { Takes the centre now the pieces are out. Plan: keep the pawns on d4 and e4, add Bf4 and a rook on c1. If Black leaves the book, push e4 and make use of the extra space. } *
